    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25669" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lăgēna</span></b>  (also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lăgaena</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lăgoena</span></b> , and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lăgōna</span></b> ),
			ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάγηνος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a large earthen vessel with a neck and handles, a
				flask, flagon, bottle</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quasi tu lagenam dicas, ubi vinum solet Chium
					esse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Curc. 1, 1, 78</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 16, 26, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 6,
				3, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2, 8, 41</span></i>; <i><span class="en">81</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">id. Ep. 2, 2, 134</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Juv. 12,
			60</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14, 271</span></i>
			et saep.—Also made of other materials, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16,
				31, 56, § 128</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Syra nigri defruti,</span>”
				<i>of glass</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					4, 46, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
